The project will be considered successful when:
- A functioning and segmented network is built in Cisco Packet Tracer.
- Appropriate security controls are implemented and tested.
- 2–3 realistic attack scenarios are modeled and investigated.
- Normal and suspicious network traffic can be analyzed using Wireshark.
- A Python-based traffic analyzer can identify and report potentially suspicious activity.
- The complete project is documented, reproducible, and explainable as a portfolio project.
